# The home skeleton's appearance preference: a fresh home is seeded with
# this the first time its owner logs in (the session's init copies it in
# if the home has none), so a new user starts with appearance settings of
# their own that the settings UI edits. It merges over the system layer
# (conf/font.msh) in fontsvc and every GUI resolves its palette + scale
# from the result.
#
#   scale     the accessibility text scale (1.0 = system size)
#   theme     dark | light
#   contrast  normal | high        (high-contrast accessibility)
#   colors    default | cb-safe    (colourblind-safe, Okabe-Ito hues)
#
# Ships a larger scale than 1.0 so the per-user push is visible on first
# login; a user lowers it (or any of these) from the settings UI.
{
  scale:    1.5
  theme:    dark
  contrast: normal
  colors:   default
}
